1. LEGAL PROTECTION UNDER GERMAN & EUROPEAN UNION LAW
This software application ("Lumin Flow: Utopia Run" / "SpaceLumin"), including all source
code, object code, executables (SpaceLumin.exe), Android packages (APK), 3D procedural
geometries, planetary surface algorithms, audio synthesis engines, UI designs, and proprietary
mathematical/AI architectures, is protected under:
  (a) German Copyright Act (Urheberrechtsgesetz — UrhG):
      - §§ 69a–69g UrhG (Besondere Bestimmungen für Computerprogramme / Protection of Computer Programs)
      - § 2 Abs. 1 Nr. 1, 2, 4, 6 UrhG (Protected Literary, Musical, Artistic & Audiovisual Works)
      - §§ 87a–87e UrhG (Schutz des Datenbankherstellers / Database Maker Rights)
      - §§ 95a–95d UrhG (Schutz technischer Maßnahmen & Informationen für die Rechtewahrnehmung)
  (b) European Union Directives & Regulations:
      - Directive 2009/24/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on the legal protection of computer programs
      - Directive 2001/29/EC (InfoSoc Directive) Art. 2, 3, 4, 6, and 7
      - Directive (EU) 2019/790 (DSM Directive) Art. 4(3) — Express Opt-Out from Text & Data Mining (TDM)
  (c) International Treaties:
      - Berne Convention for the Protection of Literary and Artistic Works & WIPO Copyright Treaty (WCT).

2. STRICT PROHIBITION OF CLONING, REPRODUCTION, DECOMPILATION & SALE (§ 69c UrhG)
Without the prior express written consent of Lumin Flow Studios, it is strictly prohibited to:
  (a) Reproduce, clone, mirror, frame, or copy this software or website in whole or in part (§ 69c Nr. 1 UrhG);
  (b) Translate, adapt, modify, decompile, disassemble, or reverse-engineer the software or its mathematical algorithms (§§ 69c Nr. 2, 69e UrhG);
  (c) Distribute, sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or make the software publicly available on any third-party website, store, or server (§ 69c Nr. 3, 4 UrhG);
  (d) Perform automated Text and Data Mining (TDM), web scraping, or AI/ML dataset extraction (Express Opt-Out pursuant to § 44b Abs. 3 UrhG & Art. 4(3) Directive (EU) 2019/790; machine-readable header: tdm-reservation: 1);
  (e) Circumvent any effective technological protection measure (§ 95a UrhG) or remove/alter any electronic Rights Management Information or digital watermark (§ 95c UrhG).

3. CIVIL & CRIMINAL ENFORCEMENT (§§ 97, 106, 108a UrhG)
Any unauthorized cloning, commercial sale, or infringement of this software triggers immediate
civil liability for injunctive relief (Unterlassung), destruction of infringing copies (Vernichtung,
§ 98 UrhG), and full damages / profit disgorgement (Schadensersatz, § 97 Abs. 2 UrhG), as well as
criminal prosecution under §§ 106, 108a, and 108b UrhG (punishable by imprisonment of up to 3 years,
or up to 5 years for commercial infringement under § 108a UrhG).

